docs/controller-service-contract.md:73:| `search_knowledge(payload)` | `KnowledgeQuery` → `KnowledgeResult`; synchronous, local lexical retrieval |
docs/MULTIMODAL_CONTRACTS.md:17:| Policy Evidence | [Knowledge/Data](controller-knowledge-contract.md), [Document](controller-document-contract.md) | Fixed demo corpus, lexical search, source hashes | Owner-scoped retrieval with page citations and grounded explanation |
docs/MULTIMODAL_CONTRACTS.md:30:| Current | `/care/requests`, `/agents/graph`, `/agents/runs`, `/live/tokens`, `/live/tool-calls`, `/voice/*`, `/knowledge/search` | Pydantic models and generated [OpenAPI](openapi.json); domain docs cover dynamic results and streaming |
docs/VALIDATION.md:39:- Real owner-policy ingestion and vector RAG: the current retrieval baseline is lexical and searches only the demo schedule and adapted terms under `synthetic_demo`. Legacy book collections and OpenAI/Chroma indexes remain excluded.
docs/controller-knowledge-contract.md:7:`POST /api/v1/knowledge/search` → **200** `KnowledgeResult`.
docs/controller-knowledge-contract.md:9:Schema: `KnowledgeQuery`.
docs/controller-knowledge-contract.md:11:<!-- schema: KnowledgeQuery -->
docs/controller-knowledge-contract.md:15:  "top_k": 3,
docs/controller-knowledge-contract.md:23:| `top_k` | 1–5, default 3 |
docs/controller-knowledge-contract.md:26:There are no upload, document-selection, collection-selection or actual-policy scopes. Additional fields are rejected. Search runs locally using English lexical matching and a small synonym list; it makes no model/network call and stores no query. Translate a non-English question in a separately consented flow before using this endpoint if needed.
docs/controller-knowledge-contract.md:33:| `method` | `lexical` |
docs/controller-knowledge-contract.md:36:| `status` | `evidence_found` or `no_evidence` |
docs/controller-knowledge-contract.md:37:| `evidence` | At most `top_k` evidence records; empty when nothing matches |
docs/controller-knowledge-contract.md:40:Each evidence record has `evidence_id`, `source_id`, `source_path`, `source_sha256`, `section`, `title`, `snippet`, `synthetic: true`, `score`. The source ID is `pawse-demo-policy` or `pawse-demo-avb`. Snippets are exact source sections or serialized JSON sections, up to 4,000 characters. Scores are lexical relevance, not probability or coverage confidence.
docs/controller-knowledge-contract.md:42:Frontend shows title, section, snippet and the demo label together. A downstream reasoning module must keep the source ID/hash with any derived claim and treat retrieved text as data. `evidence_found` only establishes a lexical match; it does not guarantee a complete answer. `no_evidence` requires an explicit absence of evidence, not an invented clause.
docs/controller-knowledge-contract.md:55:`knowledge.search(payload: KnowledgeQuery) -> KnowledgeResult` is the HTTP wrapper. It calls `search_knowledge(payload)` and maps source errors to a safe 503. Internal callers may use the same service function directly, but must handle its source errors themselves.
docs/controller-knowledge-contract.md:105:**Proposed v1 — not implemented.** Preserve `/knowledge/search` exactly as the current demo-only API. Introduce a separate `POST /api/v1/cases/{case_id}/evidence/search` only after the [Case](controller-case-contract.md) and [Document](controller-document-contract.md) controllers enforce ownership, reviewed sources and deletion. Evidence/data owns retrieval; orchestration validates the handoff.
docs/controller-knowledge-contract.md:112:  "top_k": 3,
docs/controller-knowledge-contract.md:118:`query` is 1–1,000 characters; `top_k` is 1–5; `answer_language` is `en`, `zh`, `de` or `hi`. `share_with_gemini` is a required boolean: false performs local evidence retrieval only; true permits translated-query preparation and grounded answer generation from the retrieved passages. Never send the whole private corpus when selected excerpts suffice. Scope comes from the case, not from a client-selected collection ID.
docs/controller-knowledge-contract.md:126:| `status` | `evidence_found`, `no_evidence` or `partial` |
docs/controller-knowledge-contract.md:127:| `method` | `lexical` or `lexical_with_gemini_synthesis` |
docs/API_CONTRACT.md:11:Public mode caps selected POST requests at 60 per session and 600 per process per rolling hour by default. Limits are configurable with `PAWSE_SESSION_CALLS_PER_HOUR` and `PAWSE_TOTAL_CALLS_PER_HOUR`. Covered prefixes are `/care/requests`, `/clinics/`, `/agents/runs`, `/voice/`, `/live/` and `/knowledge/search`; rejected validation/provider requests also consume an admitted attempt. Knowledge search is local but is currently included. The quota counts HTTP requests, not tokens, audio duration or provider spend; a Live token's subsequent provider audio stream is outside this HTTP counter. State resets on restart and is not shared across workers/instances.
docs/API_CONTRACT.md:30:| POST | `/knowledge/search` | Cited lexical search of the fixed synthetic insurance corpus |
docs/API_CONTRACT.md:124:`POST /knowledge/search` accepts `{ "query": "home visit surcharge 1.2.5", "top_k": 3, "scope": "synthetic_demo" }`. `top_k` is 1–5. It performs local English lexical retrieval over the reviewed demo policy and English AVB, without an embedding call or owner-document upload.
docs/API_CONTRACT.md:126:The result carries `synthetic: true`, `method: "lexical"`, `insurance_approval: "not_obtained"`, a corpus version, `evidence_found`/`no_evidence` status and evidence entries with source path/hash, clause or JSON section, exact snippet and relevance score. The score is not coverage confidence. No request may choose an arbitrary file, collection or live-policy scope. See the [RAG contract](RAG_CONTRACT.md).
docs/MULTIMODAL_ARCHITECTURE.md:21:| Policy Evidence Agent | Retrieval + `gemini-3.8-flash` synthesis | Question + reviewed policy evidence → cited explanation, gaps and questions for the insurer | Current search is lexical over a demo schedule and adapted real terms. Private-document indexing and grounded synthesis are proposed. |
docs/MULTIMODAL_ARCHITECTURE.md:35:4. **Retrieve within the case.** Query only that owner's reviewed corpus. Start with lexical retrieval; add embeddings when corpus size or evaluation justifies them. Use matching model/version vectors for indexing and queries.
docs/controller-crawling-contract.md:102:Public clinic evidence stays separate from `synthetic_demo` insurance knowledge and owner-private documents. Do not put clinic data into `/knowledge/search`'s fixed policy corpus.
docs/controller-frontend-contract.md:31:| Demo policy evidence | `POST /knowledge/search` | 200 `KnowledgeResult` | Show synthetic scope, exact snippets and citations |
docs/MODEL_ALLOCATION.md:42:The knowledge module uses lexical retrieval. A future vector index can start with the already accessible `gemini-embedding-001`, but needs a retrieval evaluation. Never mix legacy OpenAI vectors with Gemini vectors; record model, dimension, corpus hash and version, and isolate each owner's documents. Embeddings are optional for the small demo corpus.
docs/RAG_CONTRACT.md:5:The first retrieval agent is implemented in `pawse/knowledge.py`. It searches the existing **fictional demo insurance corpus** locally, returns citations, and makes no model or network calls. It is a lexical retrieval baseline with English token matching and a small synonym list, not an embedding or semantic RAG implementation.
docs/RAG_CONTRACT.md:9:`POST /api/v1/knowledge/search`
docs/RAG_CONTRACT.md:14:  "top_k": 3,
docs/RAG_CONTRACT.md:19:`query` must contain 1–1,000 characters after trimming. `top_k` is 1–5 and defaults to 3. Only `synthetic_demo` is accepted. Additional fields, file paths, collection names, and other scopes are rejected. Queries are not stored or sent to a provider.
docs/RAG_CONTRACT.md:23:The response contains `scope`, `synthetic: true`, `method: "lexical"`, `insurance_approval: "not_obtained"`, `corpus_version`, `status`, `evidence`, and a demo disclaimer. `status` is `evidence_found` or `no_evidence`. Empty results carry no generated answer. No response is a binding insurance decision.
docs/RAG_CONTRACT.md:43:Use `search_knowledge(KnowledgeQuery(query=english_query, top_k=3))` directly inside the Python orchestrator, or call the HTTP endpoint from another service. Keep retrieval concurrent with independent clinic discovery. Translate non-English questions before retrieval if needed; Chinese, Hindi, and German semantic search are not implemented here.
docs/RAG_CONTRACT.md:57:The retrieval module includes this contract, the reviewed corpus and evaluation queries. Next, add a user-owned policy ingestion flow with tenant isolation, document consent, edition/date metadata, deletion, and citations to the uploaded page or section. That corpus must use a separate authenticated scope; never replace the synthetic files with private owner documents. Evaluate lexical retrieval before adding embeddings. An embedding change requires re-indexing the corpus and recording the model and vector dimensions; the imported legacy Chroma collections cannot be assumed compatible.
docs/images/README.md:31:| `policy_evidence` | Separate lexical search under `synthetic_demo` | Existing foundation for proposed private-document retrieval and synthesis |
docs/WEB_AGENT_INTEGRATION.md:11:| Policy evidence | `POST /api/v1/knowledge/search` | Explicit demo-policy panel; English lexical search and original citations. No private-policy ingestion or coverage approval. |
docs/GEMINI_LIVE.md:53:| `search_policy` | `/knowledge/search` (demo corpus, cited) | `KnowledgeResult` |
docs/AGENT_DEVELOPMENT.md:33:| Future vector retrieval | `gemini-embedding-001` | `embedContent` returned HTTP 200 with an embedding | Retrieval pipeline; the current small demo corpus can use deterministic lexical retrieval without a vector database. |
docs/AGENT_DEVELOPMENT.md:49:| RAG/data → frontend or future coordinator | `/api/v1/knowledge/search` | Cited synthetic corpus results; not actual policy approval. Live policy ingestion is later work. |
docs/controller-live-contract.md:63:| `search_policy` | `question`: 1–1,000 characters | `search_knowledge(KnowledgeQuery)`; fixed demo corpus | `KnowledgeResult` |
docs/DATA_SOURCES.md:14:| `pawse/knowledge.py` | Working local lexical retrieval service | No credentials, uploads, network calls, or vector database needed |
docs/DEMO_STORY.md:60:| Document + Policy Evidence | Extract policy/invoice facts; retrieve clauses with page/source references | Demo lexical retrieval exists. Private-document upload, scoped indexing and grounded synthesis are planned. |

